metric in normal coordinates: g_uu = 1 + c v^2, g_uv = -c u v, g_vv = 1 + c u^2 with c = (sin^2 theta - theta^2)/theta^4
c(theta) = (sin^2 theta - theta^2)/theta^4 -> -1/3 as theta -> 0: True ; Taylor: 2/45*tt^6 - 1/3*tt^4
g = delta - (1/3) (v^2, -uv; -uv, u^2) to second order; check at (u, v) = (0.1, 0.2): [True, True, True, True]
Christoffel symbols at the pole (limit along u = v -> 0): [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0] -> all zero: True
Gamma^u_vv at (u, v) = (0.3, 0): 0.19643070336091512 (small, O(theta))
